id=a52sxq_remaster_models
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Gallery Remaster AI HDR models
author=kusti420
description=Gallery > Remaster (PhotoRemasterService) runs at SEC_FLOATING_FEATURE_SAIV_CONFIG_AI_REVITAL_VERSION=1.9,4 (the S26 Ultra value), i.e. feature level REMASTER_V4, whose EnhanceTypeSelectorV4 always applies AI HDR (HDR__DENOISE / HDR__DEBLUR / HDR__MULTI_FRAME_DEBLUR). libmidas_DNNInterface resolves the HDR models from /vendor/etc/midas/midas_config.json by ro.soc.model: SM7325 -> SRIBMidas_aiHDR_Global/Local_INT16_V430_sm7325_snpe1502.dlc (SNPE 1.50.2 on the cDSP through the vendor SNAP HAL). unica/patches/legacy replaces the target's /vendor/etc/midas with the portable a73xqxx set, which has no Qualcomm .dlc files, so the HDR model read fails ("model file length = 0", AIhdr::Init DNN Initialize Error 3) and AIhdr::DeInit frees an uninitialised pointer -> SIGABRT of photoremasterservice on every Remaster. The stock A52s vendor (A528BXXU5FWK4, the same vendor this ROM ships) has exactly these two files and used them on One UI 6 (its config maps a52sxq to them, HDR is in SAIV_CONFIG_MIDAS). This patch copies them from the extracted target firmware, plus the default-path quality models the One UI 9 config names that the portable set lacks (MQA noise/blur under their One UI 9 names, IQA, FiQA V100, moire_detection). The install runs from target/a52sxq/post_mods.sh, after unica/patches/legacy has replaced the directory; customize.sh only checks the sources so a missing firmware fails the build early. Nothing is kept in git: the files come from out/fw (target and source firmware).
